From b73d0a3add799e8be2c7d19d77e61cae694eb0f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:21:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(outcome): isolate card reads from sidebar borrowers
 [daveey]

Why: bounded shared-reader admission exposed ordinary sidebar enrichment contention as card_read_failed. Outcome evidence used the same retained connection, and the Python borrow failure lacked SQLITE_BUSY so existing retry/last-good handling did not recognize it.

Own the short lean read transaction through the existing generation-safe opener and close it deterministically. Keep the 500ms SQLite/lifecycle budget and shared per-request retry deadline. Classify remaining cached-borrow exhaustion as typed busy; no timeout increases or stale-as-confirmed outcome changes.

Proof: held real sidebar borrower through hermes_state_outcome._live_work fails for running and human-blocked cards on parent, passes after independent read. Zero-budget borrow error classifier fails on parent and passes as typed busy. Focused outcome/parity/contention suites and full scripts/check pass. Broad consumers retained separately.
---
 hermes_cli/kanban_reader_lifecycle.py         |  4 +--
 hermes_cli/kanban_session_outcome_tasks.py    |  8 ++++--
 .../test_kanban_content_key_busy_budget.py    | 13 +++++++++
 .../test_kanban_session_outcome_tasks.py      | 28 +++++++++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 49 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

